First production app (jwc-shortener, live at 1kb.uz) validated the
deploy story and surfaced concrete gaps. Added a findings→phase map
section and folded each into its phase:

- Phase 2: lint warnings in the default build path (unused RateLimit
  middleware shipped unnoticed, leaving an endpoint unthrottled)
- Phase 3: typed UniqueViolation catch (slug PK collision = generic
  500 today); substring/take builtin gaps
- Phase 4: [1.0-blocker] atomic 'update ... set col = col + 1' —
  whole-row read-modify-write loses hit counts under concurrency
- Phase 5: response-phase middleware (latency/status unobservable),
  trusted-proxy client_ip(), /readyz motivated by DB-blind healthz
- Phase 8: official Docker image + musl static builds (glibc
  mismatch pain), migrate-as-init-container k8s guide
- Next sprint: file findings as dogfooding-labelled issues
